  csr.build_csr(edge_index, N) -> {perm_dst int64[E], rowptr_dst int32[N+1], perm_src int64[E], rowptr_src int32[N+1]}
      stable torch.sort on int32 keys + searchsorted(out_int32); no host sync; capturable; E=0 ok.
  layer_cfg.make_cfg(conv_tp) -> LayerCfg (see CSR_READY); reference_fwd / reference_bwd / tp_edges (plain torch).
  nodetp_bwd.bwd(cfg, grad_out, x, y, w, edge_index, csr) -> (gx[N,d1], gy[E,16], gw[E,W])
      ONE fused source-centric CUDA kernel per layer (load_inline, codegen per cfg, exact fp64 CG literals):
      grid=N CTAs (one per SOURCE node), 128 threads (thread=channel u); x[n,u,:] and gx accumulators in registers;
      walks outgoing edges via perm_src/rowptr_src; per edge reads y[e], w[e,p*128+u], grad_out[dst(e)] once and emits
      gw[e] (direct store), gy[e] (warp-shuffle + 1 smem round, double-buffered, 1 __syncthreads/edge), gx at the end.
      No atomics, deterministic. Fused rather than edge-kernel + src-kernel: all three grads share the same
      g[dst]*x[src] products and g[dst] (E*d_out*8 B) is the dominant stream -> split would read it twice.
      Current stream, no host sync, capturable, E=0 -> gx zeros, gy/gw [0,*]. First derivatives only (once_differentiable).
  nodeconv.NodeConvFunction.apply(x, y, w, edge_index, csr_tuple, cfg, fwd_fn)  (forward=B's nodetp_fwd.fwd when
      results/nodetp8_fwd/READY + import ok, else reference_fwd; backward=nodetp_bwd.bwd)
  nodeconv.install(model, layers=None, fwd="auto"|"B"|"ref", csr_cache=True) -> handle ; nodeconv.uninstall(model, handle=None)
      mirrors flashtp_adapter_v2: exact-class allowlist (mace 0.3.17 conv_fusion branch), refuses already-fused/non-e3nn
      conv_tp, sets block.conv_fusion=True, conv_tp -> NodeConv(orig) (stock state_dict keys via hooks, not picklable),
      uninstall restores exact original objects (verified). Usable as a graphed7 transform:
        GR.build_backend("e3nn", transforms=[lambda m: NC.install(m)])                          # e3nn SC
        GR.build_backend("e3nn", transforms=[GR.HB.install_cueq_sc, lambda m: NC.install(m)])   # cueq SC (hybrid-like)
      CSR: layer 0 (producer) builds per call; layer 1 reuses it (same edge_index object/_version/N/capture state) ->
      one build_csr per model call, never reused across calls/capture boundaries.

